{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hypergraph","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"hypergraph.vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The oriented matrix of a directed hypergraph: rows by vertex index, a column per hyperedge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"code":"hyperedges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"init","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L97"},"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0VyACxc14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphRzlufc","roleHeading":"Initializer","title":"init(_:)"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl"]}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/init(_:)-6qyfl":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented matrix of a directed hypergraph: rows by vertex index, a column per hyperedge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"code":"hyperedges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order."}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"init(_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","abstract":[{"text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"topic"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph":{"abstract":[{"text":"A directed hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ordered pair of vertex sets, its sources (tail) and its targets (head). Gallo, Longo, Pallottino","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and Nguyen, “Directed hypergraphs and applications”, ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Discrete Applied Mathematics"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop (XGI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":" allows both)."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","title":"DirectedHypergraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"}}}